#!/bin/sh
# Refresh the index entries `pre-commit` staged into a TEMPORARY index.
#
# 🔴 **For a PATHSPEC commit — `git commit -- <paths>`, the workspace's normal
# shape — git hands `pre-commit` a temporary index and says so:**
#
#     pathspec commit : GIT_INDEX_FILE=.git/next-index-64981.lock
#     bare commit     : GIT_INDEX_FILE=.git/index
#
# So `pre-commit`'s `git add API.md API.json` reaches THIS COMMIT and never
# reaches `.git/index`. The commit then moves HEAD while the main index still
# holds the pre-commit content, and `git status` reports `MM API.md` carrying a
# diff that DELETES the docs just committed.
#
# ⚠️ **The danger is the DIRECTION, not the dirt.** A later bare `git commit`
# commits the index and silently reverts API.md/API.json — and in a checkout
# several sessions share, whoever pays is not whoever caused it. It also blocks
# every other session, because `docs:check` then compares against a tree the
# stale entry makes look wrong. Measured twice on 2026-09-05, in two sessions.
#
# ⚠️ **This cannot live in `pre-commit`: git holds `.git/index.lock` for the
# duration of the commit**, so a second `git add` against the real index there
# dies with *"Unable to create '.git/index.lock': File exists"*. Verified.
#
# A no-op after a bare commit, where the index was the real one all along.
git reset -q HEAD -- API.md API.json 2>/dev/null || true
